The Feynman Lectures on Physics, Volume II (@em-feynman: 0, is #reference, #part-of @em-sources) { r_436GYN2CVWCERX7EXFDTWX28XT
Richard P. Feynman, Robert B. Leighton and Matthew Sands. The Feynman Lectures on Physics, Volume II, New Millennium online edition. [Caltech edition](https://www.feynmanlectures.caltech.edu/) · [Volume II contents](https://www.feynmanlectures.caltech.edu/II_toc.html).

Read the complete volume as a sustained alternative physical explanation, or first read its complete assigned chapters and finish the remaining volume during advanced study. Keep a comparison notebook on fields, potentials, material models, induction, waves and the passage from macroscopic classical descriptions to microscopic physics.

The Caltech site permits free reading of copyrighted material; it is not a public-domain or CC edition. The 42-chapter contents were checked on 29 October 2026. Online access, downloadable products and permission to reproduce material are distinct. Only links and original connecting explanation are supplied here.

